UHF CCSD(TQ) SINGLE POINT ENERGY CALCULATION
H
O 1 R
H 2 R 1 A

R=1.0
A=104.

*ACES2
BASIS=DZP
CALC=CCSD(TQ),SPHERICAL=OFF,REF=UHF

REF=UHF rather than RHF because the fifth-order triples/quadruples code has
no RHF path: TRPS14, the all-alpha spin case, is skipped for IUHF=0, so the
2*(X1+X2) assembly in vcc5t/nonit3.F would silently drop about half of each
fifth-order term -- 2.24e-04 hartree here. xvcc5t now refuses that
combination outright; the comment at that assembly says what an RHF fix
would need. UHF is the same closed-shell solution for this molecule (CCSD
and CCSD(T) agree with the RHF run to 2e-09) and reproduces this case's
archive reference to 3.8e-09, so the quadruples code keeps real coverage --
it is the only case in the suite that exercises vcc5q at all.
